# Phase 5 transcript (T-U6, fx v0.0.16's 70611a91): a three-line prompt
# submitted on a full screen (the answer of p5-transcript-submit, taller than
# the screen). The terminal bytes are kept on both sides of Enter (`wire`) to
# find what the frame that clears the composer shows of the prompt: fx
# previews its last line until the card is written. `submit-0.15` is snapped
# while the fake gateway holds the answer after its first chunk (`holdAt` 1 in
# the shared turns file, `held`/`release`), no longer at 0.15 s, so both
# binaries have read the same chunk; the wire still holds every frame.
gateway p5-transcript-submit-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
wait 4
type fill the screen
wait 1
key Enter
wait 8
snap filled
paste multi line one\nmulti line two\nmulti line three
wait 0.5
wire before-submit
key Enter
held
wait 1
snap submit-0.15
release
wait 3
snap second
snapfull second
wire after-submit
gwlog
